  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is playing a game consisting of NNN rounds. In each round he rolls a regular six faced dice.\n\nHe starts with an initial score of 000. Let the number rolled by him in a particular round be XXX.\n\nIf this is not the first round and the previous number rolled was 111, Chef will add 2⋅X2 \\cdot X2⋅X to his score, otherwise he will add XXX to his score.\n\nFor example, if the game has 666 rounds and the rolls are [2,1,6,1,1,4][2, 1, 6, 1, 1, 4][2,1,6,1,1,4] in the given order, his score will be 2+1+(2⋅6)+1+(2⋅1)+(2⋅4)=262 + 1 + (2 \\cdot 6) + 1 + (2 \\cdot 1) + (2 \\cdot 4) = 262+1+(2⋅6)+1+(2⋅1)+(2⋅4)=26.\n\nFind the **maximum possible score** he can obtain after NNN rounds.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single integer NNN the number of rounds.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum score that Chef can get.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n2\n4",
        "output": "13\n26",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Chef can roll [1,6][1, 6][1,6] and his score will be 1+(2⋅6)=131 + (2 \\cdot 6) = 131+(2⋅6)=13.\nTest case 222: Chef can roll [1,6,1,6][1, 6, 1, 6][1,6,1,6] and his score will be 1+(2⋅6)+1+(2⋅6)=261 + (2 \\cdot 6) + 1 + (2 \\cdot 6) =261+(2⋅6)+1+(2⋅6)=26."
      }
    ]
  },
